        <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
        <p class="effective">Effective date: July 30, 2026</p>

        <p>Veller Partners LLC ("Veller Partners", "we", "us") respects the privacy of every visitor to this website and of every party with whom we correspond. This Privacy Policy describes the information we collect through vellerpartners.com, how we use it, and the choices available to you.</p>

        <h2>1. Information We Collect</h2>
        <p>This website is informational in nature and does not require registration. We collect personal information only when you choose to provide it, for example when you contact us by email at iv@vellerpartners.com. Such information may include your name, email address, organization, and the contents of your correspondence.</p>
        <p>Our hosting infrastructure may automatically record limited technical data, such as IP addresses, browser type, and pages visited, for security and performance purposes.</p>

        <h2>2. How We Use Information</h2>
        <p>We use the information you provide solely to respond to your inquiries, to evaluate potential business and investment relationships, to satisfy legal and regulatory obligations including know your customer and anti money laundering requirements, and to maintain the security of our systems. We do not use your information for advertising purposes.</p>

        <h2>3. Sharing and Disclosure</h2>
        <p>We do not sell, rent, or trade personal information. We may share information with professional advisers, service providers, and counterparties on a confidential basis where necessary to conduct our business, and with regulators, courts, or other authorities where disclosure is required by applicable law.</p>

        <h2>4. Data Security</h2>
        <p>We maintain administrative, technical, and organizational safeguards designed to protect personal information against unauthorized access, alteration, or destruction. No method of electronic transmission or storage is entirely secure, and we cannot guarantee absolute security.</p>

        <h2>5. Data Retention</h2>
        <p>We retain personal information only for as long as reasonably necessary to fulfil the purposes described in this Policy, to comply with legal, accounting, and regulatory requirements, and to resolve disputes.</p>

        <h2>6. Your Rights</h2>
        <p>Depending on your jurisdiction, you may have rights to access, correct, delete, or restrict the processing of your personal information. To exercise any such rights, contact us at iv@vellerpartners.com and we will respond in accordance with applicable law.</p>

        <h2>7. Cookies and Analytics</h2>
        <p>This website does not use advertising cookies. Essential technical cookies and standard infrastructure analytics may be employed by our hosting provider to ensure the website functions correctly and securely.</p>

        <h2>8. Third Party Websites</h2>
        <p>This website may contain links to third party websites. We are not responsible for the privacy practices or content of any third party, and we encourage you to review the privacy policies of any website you visit.</p>

        <h2>9. Changes to This Policy</h2>
        <p>We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. The effective date above indicates the most recent revision. Continued use of this website after any revision constitutes acceptance of the updated Policy.</p>

        <h2>10. Contact</h2>
        <p>Questions regarding this Privacy Policy or our data practices may be directed to <a href="mailto:iv@vellerpartners.com">iv@vellerpartners.com</a>.</p>
